      "detail": "cat >> docs/decisions.md <<'EOF'\n\n## D88 · Favoring root-cause fixes is a standing default, and it stays inside `small`\n\n- **Decision:** `defaults.toml` gains `root-cause`, citing the 2026-10-13 addendum in `BRIEF.md`. When a request\n  reports a failure, the fix goes where the fault originates, not at the symptom or the one instance that\n  surfaced. A cause outside the request's scope is named, with a proposed fix, not silently worked around. The\n  statement requires a fix's description to name the root cause and say why the change addresses it; that is\n  what the verifier checks. The version stays at 1: this adds an entry and changes none.\n- **Relation to `small`:** The root-cause fix is the one focused change. The default does not permit widening\n  scope, so an out-of-scope cause is reported, not fixed. The `small` entry is unchanged.\n- **Alternatives:** Fold the rule into `small` (rejected: it would change an existing entry and mix two ideas);\n  enforce it in prompts or code (out of scope for this change).\n- **Tradeoff:** The rule is prose-only. Enforcement rests on the verifier reading the fix's description, so a\n  vague description can pass unless the verifier is strict.\n- **Reversal cost:** Low. One entry and one test.\n- **Provenance:** `BRIEF.md`, Addenda, 2026-10-13: Root causes. Test in `crates/athena-data/src/defaults.rs`.\nEOF"
